            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Domestic Policy and the \"Jamahiriya\" System</strong><br>\nGaddafi introduced the \"Jamahiriya,\" or \"state of the masses,\" in Libya, which he claimed was a form of direct democracy, though in practice it was considered authoritarian, with power concentrated in his hands.</p>\n\n<p><strong>c1</strong><br>\nEarly Life and Immigrant Background</p>\n\n<p><strong>Mark Rothko, born Markus Yakovlevich Rothkowitz in 1903 in Dvinsk, Russia, immigrated to the United States with his family in 1913. Escaping Jewish persecution, they settled in Portland, Oregon, where he later attended Yale University before dropping out to pursue a career in art in New York City.</strong><br>\nIntroduction to the Art World</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
